  "一段短视频：她背靠观景台的铁护栏、两手搭在栏杆上对镜头笑，身后是层层的峡谷和蓝天白云。镜头平视、人在画面中间偏右。": "A short video. She leans back against the overlook's metal railing with both hands resting on the rail, smiling at the camera, with layer after layer of canyon, blue sky, and white clouds behind her. The camera is at eye level, and she's just right of center.",
  "Mather Point、Yavapai Point 的观景台都有这种弧形护栏。人靠在护栏里侧，拍的人站在一两米外、和眼睛差不多高，让护栏斜穿画面；上午 10 点前光从东边来，脸不会太暗。": "The overlooks at Mather Point and Yavapai Point both have curved railings like this. Lean on the inside of the railing, and have the photographer stand 3–6 feet away at about eye level, so the railing cuts diagonally across the frame. Before 10 a.m. the light comes from the east and your face won't be in shadow.",
