  "大峡谷崖边的岩石平台（帖子打了大峡谷国家公园的地点）": "A rock ledge on the rim of the Grand Canyon (the post is tagged Grand Canyon National Park)",
  "黄金周第一次去大峡谷。首图横拍：她站在一块伸向峡谷的平顶大岩石上挥手，拍的人在后方稍远处，人在画面中间、拍得很小，大片层层的峡谷和远处的地平线做背景。": "Her first visit to the Grand Canyon, during Japan's Golden Week holidays. The first photo is horizontal: she stands on a large flat-topped rock that juts out over the canyon, waving. The photographer is some distance behind her, so she's small in the center of the frame, set against layer after layer of canyon and the distant horizon.",
  "南缘各观景点都有伸出去的岩石平台，大多有护栏。拍的人退后 5–10 米横拍、把人放小，让峡谷占满画面；早上或傍晚太阳低的时候岩层最清楚。": "Every South Rim viewpoint has rock platforms that jut out, and most have railings. Have the photographer step back 15–30 feet and shoot horizontally, keeping the person small so the canyon fills the frame. The rock layers stand out best early or late in the day, when the sun is low.",
  "她站的岩石外侧没有护栏：只站在有护栏或离边缘很远的平台上，靠拍摄距离把峡谷拍大，不要为了效果走到边上。": "There's no railing on the outer side of the rock she's standing on. Stand only on platforms with a railing or well back from the edge, and let the shooting distance make the canyon look big. Don't walk to the edge for the effect.",
